From f149ce148bd597722e392664f1c8c97cf95ae568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: neurocontrarian <56934000+neurocontrarian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:27:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] win32hle: Winsock select

select(nfds, read, write, except, timeout) through poll(). Winsock's fd_set
is a count and an array of up to 64 SOCKETs, timeval two 32-bit longs, and a
NULL timeout waits for ever. Each set is rewritten to hold only its ready
sockets and the total is returned. A wait gives the machine to the other
guest threads (hle_block_begin/end).

Operation Flashpoint's multiplayer screen calls it.
